# Code owners for StudCraft.
#
# **This file is enforced.** The repository ruleset "Require PR review except
# jujorie" requires one approving review on `main` with `require_code_owner_review`
# set, and lists a single bypass actor. So a pull request from anyone else that
# touches a path below cannot merge without an owner's approval — which, while
# there is one owner, is the same thing as "only an admin may change it".
#
# The paragraph that used to sit here said the opposite: that `main` required 0
# approvals and enabling code-owner review would deadlock a solo maintainer. That
# is still true of the *branch protection* settings, and it was true when written.
# It stopped being the whole picture when the ruleset was added, because rulesets
# and branch protection are evaluated together and the more restrictive wins. A
# comment describing one layer of two reads as a description of the whole.
#
# What this file cannot do: a path restriction that blocks the push itself.
# `file_path_restriction` lives in a *push* ruleset, and GitHub refuses those on
# public repositories — "Source public repos cannot have push rules". Review is
# the mechanism available here, so the coverage below has to be complete.
#
# On the day a second maintainer joins, add them below. Two other decisions
# belong to that same day — whether the bypass actor stays, and whether a
# path-guard CI gate is finally worth its cost. `system/ci-gates.md` ("The day a
# non-admin collaborator appears") argues both, and is where they are decided.

# Everything, by default.
*                       @jujorie

# The ruleset itself. Changes here need someone who knows the design code.
/docs/                  @jujorie

# Process and design constitution.
/system/                @jujorie
/CODE_OF_DESIGN.md      @jujorie
/CONTRIBUTING.md        @jujorie
/AGENTS.md              @jujorie

# CLAUDE.md is one line: an `@AGENTS.md` import. Owning AGENTS.md and not the
# file that loads it leaves the loader free to point somewhere else.
/CLAUDE.md              @jujorie

# Agent definitions, path-scoped rules, permission allow/deny lists and the
# PreToolUse hooks that refuse an edit before CI ever sees it. This directory
# decides what every agent working on the repository is allowed to do, and it
# was the one gap in this file.
/.claude/               @jujorie

# CI gates and the release/archive automation. Breaking these silently breaks
# every other guarantee in the repo — including the review requirement that
# makes this file mean anything.
/.github/               @jujorie
/scripts/               @jujorie

# Spec deltas and archived changes.
/openspec/              @jujorie
